.TH qsh-doctor 1  "doctor 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-doctor \- Diagnose this deployment: identity, ACL policy, audit log, trust store, clock and (best\-effort) network reachability (`docs/CLI.md` §6.17). Always exits `0` on a successful run — findings are reported as data, not exit status (`overall` field); only doctor\*(Aqs own inability to run at all (e.g. no identity yet) fails the command
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh doctor\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIHOST\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Diagnose this deployment: identity, ACL policy, audit log, trust store, clock and (best\-effort) network reachability (`docs/CLI.md` §6.17). Always exits `0` on a successful run — findings are reported as data, not exit status (`overall` field); only doctor\*(Aqs own inability to run at all (e.g. no identity yet) fails the command
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit a single `qsh.cli/v1` JSON envelope on stdout instead of human\-readable text
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Emit newline\-delimited JSON on stdout (reserved for streaming commands; non\-streaming commands emit a single line, same as `\-\-json`)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase diagnostic verbosity on stderr (`\-v` info, `\-vv` debug, `\-vvv` trace). Never affects stdout (`docs/CLI.md` §2.2)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress diagnostic output on stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
[\fIHOST\fR]
Additional pinned host to probe connectivity for, beyond whatever `[reverse].controller` names
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
